The project includes locating, drilling, completing, and testing two well sites.  After rating the new
wells, they (and two other existing wells) will be connected to the BOPU Borie Wellfield and
ultimately to King II storage tank and the Cheyenne distribution system.  The additional
groundwater supply is needed to supplement BOPU water portfolio in the event of Colorado
River Curtailment and a reduction up to 15,000 acre-feet per year of Cheyenne's firm yield
supply (68% of total).
No
BOPU does not operate a regionalized system, but does serve consecutive systems (i.e., South
Cheyenne Water and Sewer District and Warren Air Force Base).  BOPU has planned for potential
rural customers to connect to its system in case of failing wells or declining water quality.
Cheyenne Belvoir Ranch Level II Study, December 2005
Belvoir Wells No. 5&6 Pumping Test Report Aquifer Impact Report, October 2007
